# Known bug: a token copy of an Aura spell is attached only to a target on the battlefield (ops::attach), so the token Animate Dead
# a copy resolves into is not attached to the creature card in the graveyard it targeted (CR 707.10f, 608.3b, 303.4a) and is put away at once.
# Uldaros Theorix exiles Animate Dead and Black Lotus from Bot1's graveyard; an Ornithopter (a creature card) is also in the
# graveyard, left alone: the Animate Dead copy has a legal target, is offered, and is cast, choosing the Ornithopter card as
# its target (CR 303.4). The Aura spell copy resolves into a token Animate Dead (CR 707.10f) and the Ornithopter comes
# back under Bot1's control, enchanted by it - the positive control of the neighbouring scenario, where no creature card gave the
# copy a target and it was not offered. It costs 2 of the six, and the Lotus 0.

